   "he": "קָדָשִׁים קַלִּים נֶאֱכָלִים [בְּכׇל מַחֲנֵה יִשְׂרָאֵל]. אָמַר רַב הוּנָא: בְּכׇל מְקוֹמוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל, אֲבָל מַחֲנֶה לָא הָוֵי.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that once the Tabernacle was established in the wilderness, «offerings of lesser sanctity» were «eaten throughout the camp of Israel. Rav Huna says:» This means that offerings of lesser sanctity were eaten «in any» of the «places» that «an Israelite» would be found. «But there was no» actual «camp,» outside of which it was prohibited to eat the offerings."
  }
